  slide "G · Dispatch materialization" {
    eyebrow: "MATERIALIZATION · STEP 3 — ON THE HOT PATH"
    title: "Materialize = concatenate pre-serialized bytes"
    lede: "Content is never re-serialized on the request path — dispatch just splices byte spans."
    narration: "Component G, materialization step 3 — on the hot path. Materialize means concatenate pre-serialized bytes: content is never re-serialized on the request path, dispatch just splices byte spans. Turn::dispatch_body has a precedence — raw, then token-ids, then messages, first present wins. format_prepared_payload walks a BodyPlan, an ordered list of byte spans — static segments interleaved with dynamic splices and media URLs — and concat produces a contiguous request body carried as HttpRequest.request_body_bytes. The byte-exact fast path uses request_body_bytes; request_body as a Value is only kept for accuracy runs. Media resolves through SyntheticMediaPublisher — inline data-URI, or a content-server URL spliced as a dynamic span."
    caption: "Splice byte spans · BodyPlan concat · never re-serialize."
