        after gi-title reveal gi-sub duration 160
        after gi-sub reveal gi-graph duration 320
        after gi-graph reveal gi-gate-label duration 140
        after gi-gate-label stagger targets [gi-gates-1, gi-gates-2] step 90 duration 180
        after gi-gates-2 reveal gi-chan-label duration 140
        after gi-chan-label reveal gi-chan duration 200
      }
    }
  }

  slide "J · Lowering and execution" {
    eyebrow: "LOWERING AND EXECUTION"
    title: "From authored or recorded, into one executor"
    lede: "Two lowering paths converge on a single TraceExecutor that fires each node."
    narration: "Component J, lowering and execution — from authored or recorded, into one executor. Two lowering paths: dag_jsonl goes through GraphBuilder, turning FORK, SPAWN, and JOIN into nodes, edges, and channels; traces go through the LCP-trie lowerer, a content-parent trie with idle-warp and interval-order fan-in. Then one TraceExecutor fires each node: await_inputs as a fan-in gate, gate delay, splice which snapshots channels, materialize the prompt, admission, and dispatch, which publishes and advances to the next. Three trace formats: WEKA is recursive JSON with heuristic boundaries that honors max_osl; Dynamo lowers sessions to chains to trees with a subagent depth guard; aiperf_trace is strict v1 with ground-truth tags and block_lens."
    caption: "Two lowering paths · one TraceExecutor · three trace formats."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "le-badge", variant = "rect", label = "J", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
