  slide "K · Metrics core" {
    eyebrow: "METRICS CORE"
    title: "A declarative catalog into a NaN-sparse store"
    lede: "Validated for uniqueness, dependency tiering and acyclicity — pinned with a stable catalog fingerprint."
    narration: "Component K — metrics core: a declarative catalog into a NaN-sparse store. The catalog has 119 rows — 103 Python identities plus 16 native sweep identities — validated for uniqueness, dependency tiering, and acyclicity, then pinned with a stable catalog fingerprint. MetricType is Record, Aggregate, or Derived. The ColumnStore treats NaN as absence, aligned by absolute request index, with CSR ragged series for in-context-learning shots. The ingest-to-derive pipeline runs NativeMetricsObserver, RecordIngest, Accumulator, then derived metrics in topological order. TTFT, ITL, TPOT, end-to-end, and goodput compute Rayon-parallel above 4096 rows; sweep-lines give concurrency and tokens-in-flight curves."
    caption: "119-row catalog · NaN-sparse ColumnStore · ingest → derive."
