  slide "K · RaggedSeries" {
    eyebrow: "COLUMNSTORE · RAGGED BACKEND"
    title: "RaggedSeries — a CSR list backend for ICL"
    lede: "Variable-length per-record series stored in one contiguous buffer with row offsets — no per-row allocation."
    narration: "Component K, the ragged ColumnStore backend — RaggedSeries, a CSR list backend for in-context-learning shots. Variable-length per-record series live in one contiguous values arena plus an offsets vector, so a ragged row is a slice, never a heap-allocated Vec. Row i equals values from indptr[i] to indptr[i+1]; an indptr of zero, three, four, seven reconstructs record zero of length three, record one of length one, and record two of length three. It sits beside NumericColumn, where NaN marks absence, in the same absolute-request-index alignment. append_store merges worker shards by concatenating buffers and shifting offsets. Sweep-lines read the ragged ICL series directly for tokens-in-flight and concurrency curves."
    caption: "CSR values arena + indptr · row = slice · append_store shifts offsets."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "rs-badge", variant = "rect", label = "K", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
      sdk.Label(id = "rs-badge-l", text = "K", x = 123, y = 48.6, width = 86.4, height = 54, inkRole = theme(ink.primary))
