  slide "L · Reporting and export" {
    eyebrow: "REPORTING AND EXPORT"
    title: "One authoritative report, a fan-out of exporters"
    lede: "Sole atomic create_new + rename; the registry orders local-file writers before network uploaders, all best-effort."
    narration: "Component L — reporting and export: one authoritative report, a fan-out of exporters. NativeReport is schema_version 2.0 — run, summary, metrics, server_metrics, accuracy, and errors, with finite-or-absent values. It is written once through a sole atomic path: refuse if exists, temp create_new, then atomic rename, before run_exporters. The registry orders local-file writers first — GenaiPerfV1, ConsoleTxt, Timeslice, AccuracyCsv, ServerMetrics, and Parquet — then network uploaders Otel, Mlflow, and Wandb, all best-effort. GenaiPerfV1 is byte-for-byte versus the retired Python emitter, and ConsoleTxt reproduces Rich box geometry; run_exporters logs and never aborts the run."
    caption: "Atomic create_new + rename · local writers before network uploaders."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "rp-badge", variant = "rect", label = "L", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
