  slide "N · Accuracy" {
    eyebrow: "ACCURACY"
    title: "Rust drives, a Python worker grades"
    lede: "Accuracy is not a dispatch workload — problems flow through the ordinary online scheduler, transport and observer."
    narration: "Component N — accuracy: Rust drives, a Python worker grades. Accuracy is not a dispatch workload; problems flow through the ordinary online scheduler, transport, and observer. Rust owns scheduling, IO and timing, and metrics; the Python Lighteval worker owns dataset prep and prompts, hidden tests, and grading. They talk over EVALUATOR_PROTOCOL_VERSION one — versioned JSONL over stdio, env_clear plus an allowlist, and data-hiding by deny_unknown_fields. Problems are graded in batches, joined by AccuracyAccumulator, giving a Wilson confidence interval, accuracy-at-load, and correct-answers-per-kWh drawn from the telemetry sidecar's energy metric."
    caption: "Rust owns scheduling/IO/metrics · Python worker grades over versioned stdio."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "ac-badge", variant = "rect", label = "N", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
