  slide "O · Side-channel telemetry" {
    eyebrow: "SIDE-CHANNEL TELEMETRY"
    title: "Four Clock-injected sources, one metric series"
    lede: "Continuous scrapes dedup identical bodies into gauge distributions; boundary scrapes give exact reset-clamped counter deltas."
    narration: "Component O — side-channel telemetry: four Clock-injected sources, one metric series. Continuous scrapes dedup identical bodies into gauge distributions; boundary scrapes give exact reset-clamped counter deltas. The four sources are gpu_telemetry, a DCGM-first source with per-GPU energy, power, and efficiency joins; network_latency, a fresh-TCP-connect RTT calibration with per-target stats; server_metrics, a Prometheus parser over a vLLM and SGLang atlas with boundary deltas; and content_server, an Axum server that turns images and videos into stable HTTP URLs. All four converge as SidecarMetric, a shared series into the native report, barrier-synchronized to phases as ScheduledPhaseSidecars."
    caption: "gpu_telemetry · network_latency · server_metrics · content_server → SidecarMetric."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "oc-badge", variant = "rect", label = "O", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
