  slide "P · Cellular" {
    eyebrow: "CELLULAR MULTI-PROCESS"
    title: "A controller spawns N cells, merges one report"
    lede: "The union of ordinals is validated as a permutation of 0..total, stable-sorted and re-ingested — byte-identical to a single-cell run."
    narration: "Component P — cellular multi-process: a controller spawns N cells and merges one report. The union of ordinals is validated as a permutation of zero to total, stable-sorted and re-ingested, byte-identical to a single-cell run. Partition uses ModuloCellPartition with isolated stream roots; issuance uses a global ordinal, never a shared atomic; shards are raw RecordIngest over MessagePack carrying NaN and plus-infinity; heartbeats carry live t-digest percentiles for a progress lane. It is fail-closed: HTTP transport only, synthetic single-turn, request-bounded phases, requests at least cell_count — it rejects duration, sessions, adaptive, and multi-turn."
    caption: "controller → N cells → merged report · byte-identical · fail-closed."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "ce-badge", variant = "rect", label = "P", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
      sdk.Label(id = "ce-badge-l", text = "P", x = 123, y = 48.6, width = 86.4, height = 54, inkRole = theme(ink.primary))
      sdk.Caption(id = "ce-kicker", text = "CELLULAR MULTI-PROCESS", x = 236.4, y = 54, width = 1350, height = 48.6, inkRole = theme(accent.primary))
