  slide "Q · Dynosim" {
    eyebrow: "DYNOSIM CO-SIMULATION"
    title: "Co-simulate Dynamo in-process, no sockets"
    lede: "AIPerf owns clock, workload, observers and report; dynamo-mocker owns scheduler and perf-model behind SteppableReplay."
    narration: "Component Q — Dynosim co-simulation: co-simulate Dynamo in-process, with no sockets. AIPerf owns the clock, workload, observers, and report; dynamo-mocker owns the scheduler and perf-model behind SteppableReplay. Two modes differ only in the clock and driver axis: dynosim_offline runs a Sim clock through drive_sim_with_source with enforced byte-exact parity versus Dynamo, while dynosim_online runs a Real clock through drive_real_with_source with relaxed parity. DynosimSink reuses the same RequestSink, HttpRequestDispatcher, and TurnDispatcher seams; EngineHost bridges the DES or wall clock as a SimEventSource; token priority is raw_token_ids, then trace_hash_ids, then chat body. It requires worker_count equal to one; dynamo-full adds the router, ZMQ, KV, and AIC surface."
    caption: "offline byte-exact vs online relaxed · same sink seams · worker_count == 1."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "dy-badge", variant = "rect", label = "Q", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
      sdk.Label(id = "dy-badge-l", text = "Q", x = 123, y = 48.6, width = 86.4, height = 54, inkRole = theme(ink.primary))
