  slide "R · Mock server" {
    eyebrow: "MOCK SERVER"
    title: "A deterministic, standalone inference target"
    lede: "OpenAI / Anthropic / TGI-compatible; Python does not supervise it — it supplies an ordinary online URL."
    narration: "Component R — the mock server: a deterministic, standalone inference target. It is OpenAI, Anthropic, and TGI-compatible; Python does not supervise it — it simply supplies an ordinary online URL. It offers two latency models over goodput versus offered load: an analytic curve and a queue-threshold model whose goodput batch-collapses past the queue threshold. Server features include a prefix cache with SGLang-style eviction over chain-hash blocks, a DCGM faker producing 100 Hz throughput-driven per-GPU telemetry, TCP_NODELAY over a manual accept loop with no Nagle on SSE chunks, and a --fast mode with zero latency and no scheduler or cache. It emits seven Prometheus dialects, including vllm, sglang, trtllm, and dynamo families."
    caption: "Deterministic OpenAI/Anthropic/TGI target · two latency models · 7 dialects."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "ms-badge", variant = "rect", label = "R", x = 123, y = 32.4, width = 86.4, height = 86.4, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
      sdk.Label(id = "ms-badge-l", text = "R", x = 123, y = 48.6, width = 86.4, height = 54, inkRole = theme(ink.primary))
